of rings on <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>presheaf of <MATH_0006>-modules <MATH_0007>\non <MATH_0008><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a presheaf of abelian groups on\n<MATH_0009> together with a morphism of presheaves\nof sets <MATH_0010>\nsuch that for all <MATH_0011> the map\n<MATH_0012>\nturns the group <MATH_0013> into an <MATH_0014>-module.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism <MATH_0015>\nof presheaves of <MATH_0016>-modules on <MATH_0017><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis a morphism of abelian presheaves on <MATH_0018>\nwhich induces an <MATH_0019>-module homomorphism\n<MATH_0020> for every <MATH_0021>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Suppose that <MATH_0022> is a sheaf of rings\non <MATH_0023>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0003>sheaf <MATH_0024> of <MATH_0025>-modules\non <MATH_0026><TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is a presheaf of <MATH_0027>-modules\non <MATH_0028> whose underlying presheaf of abelian groups\nis a sheaf.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a6028278c621b32e6d5db52114c9a27a1d29faf1d8cb4a6d5e65a742a25e4f37", "unit_id": "tag:009S:statement"}
